    <div class="sh-body">
      <div class="sh-num">02</div>
      <h2>Choose USPS or FedEx</h2>
      <p>Either one works. Both give away a small box for free, and that's what we suggest for the outside. <strong>Your own sturdy box is fine too.</strong> Each carrier uses a different address, so use the one that matches.</p>
      <div class="sh-carriers">
        <div class="sh-carrier">
          <div class="sh-carrier__name">USPS</div>
          <div class="sh-carrier__box">Free box: <b>Priority Mail Small Flat Rate</b></div>
          <address class="sh-addr" id="addr-usps"><small>Ship to</small>Tony Gryckiewicz<br>PO Box 10575<br>Lancaster, PA 17605</address>
          <button type="button" class="sh-copy" data-copy="addr-usps">Copy address</button>
        </div>
        <div class="sh-carrier">
          <div class="sh-carrier__name">FedEx</div>
          <div class="sh-carrier__box">Free box: <b>FedEx Small box</b></div>
          <address class="sh-addr" id="addr-fedex"><small>Ship to</small>Tony Gryckiewicz<br>1851 Colonial Village Lane<br>Lancaster, PA 17601</address>
          <button type="button" class="sh-copy" data-copy="addr-fedex">Copy address</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sh-carrier__warn">FedEx can't deliver to a PO Box, so FedEx packages go to the street address only.</p>
    </div>
  </li>

